 "sentences": [
  {
   "text": "Pablo Escobar's hippos are still alive, and Colombia has approved killing some of them.",
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 5.1
  },
  {
   "text": "In 1981, he imported four of them for his private zoo.",
   "start": 5.78,
   "end": 9.02
  },
  {
   "text": "His estate lay between Medell\u00edn and Bogot\u00e1.",
   "start": 9.02,
   "end": 11.86
  },
  {
   "text": "After he died in 1993, they escaped and spread.",
   "start": 12.36,
   "end": 15.64
  },
  {
   "text": "By 2007 there were sixteen, by 2014 about forty, and now around two hundred.",
   "start": 16.32,
   "end": 21.92
  },
  {
   "text": "In April 2026, Colombia approved killing more than eighty of them.",
   "start": 22.38,
   "end": 26.16
  },
  {
   "text": "An Indian billionaire offered to take them to India instead.",
   "start": 26.16,
   "end": 29.06
  },
  {
   "text": "Most conservationists call them invasive, but some ecologists say they should stay.",
   "start": 30.16,
   "end": 34.28
  },
  {
   "text": "So who decides what happens to Escobar's hippos?",
   "start": 35.1,
   "end": 37.74
  }
 ]
